    54	| 0 | float32 | 4 |
    55	| 1 | float64 | 8 |
    56	| 2 | float16 | 2 |
    57	| 3 | int32 | 4 |
    58	| 4 | int64 | 8 |
    59	| 5 | bfloat16 | 2 |
    60	
    61	**Validation**: `DataSize` must equal `product(Shape) * element_byte_size`. If it does not match, the tensor block is malformed.
    62	
    63	### 1.3 Metadata Section
    64	
    65	Located at `MetadataOffset`. Contains `NumMetadata` key-value pairs:
    66	
    67	| Size | Type | Field | Description |
    68	|------|------|-------|-------------|
    69	| 2 | uint16 | KeyLen | Length of key |
    70	| KeyLen | bytes | Key | UTF-8 key string |
    71	| 4 | uint32 | ValueLen | Length of value |
    72	| ValueLen | bytes | Value | UTF-8 value (JSON-encoded) |
    73	
    74	Common metadata keys:
    75	- `model_name`: string, the model architecture name
    76	- `dataset`: string, training dataset identifier
    77	- `training_config`: JSON object with hyperparameters
    78	- `notes`: string, free-form notes
    79	
    80	### 1.4 Provenance Section
    81	
[?2004hroot@n30009:/app# nl -ba docs/formats.md | sed -n '121,181p'
[?2004l   121	```json
   122	{
   123	  "ts": "2024-01-15T10:30:00Z",
   124	  "epoch": 1,
   125	  "step": 1000,
   126	  "loss": 0.5234,
   127	  "lr": 0.001,
   128	  "grad_norm": 1.23,
   129	  "acc": 0.8200,
   130	  "event": "step"
   131	}
   132	```
   133	
   134	### Required Fields
   135	
   136	| Field | Type | Description |
   137	|-------|------|-------------|
   138	| `ts` | string | ISO 8601 timestamp (UTC, `Z` suffix required) |
   139	| `epoch` | integer | Current training epoch (0-indexed) |
   140	| `step` | integer | Global training step (monotonically increasing within an epoch) |
   141	
   142	### Optional Metric Fields
   143	
   144	| Field | Type | Description |
   145	|-------|------|-------------|
   146	| `loss` | float | Training loss |
   147	| `lr` | float | Learning rate |
   148	| `grad_norm` | float | Gradient L2 norm |
   149	| `acc` | float | Accuracy metric (0.0 to 1.0) |
   150	| `event` | string | Event type: `step`, `epoch_end`, `checkpoint`, `eval` |
   151	
   152	### Shard Semantics
   153	
   154	- Multiple shard files may exist in the same evidence directory
   155	- Shards may have overlapping `(epoch, step)` ranges
   156	- Shards are named arbitrarily (any `.jsonl` filename is valid)
   157	- Lines within a single shard are not guaranteed to be in chronological order
   158	- Malformed lines (invalid JSON) should be silently skipped with a count in verbose output
   159	
   160	---
   161	
   162	## 3. Configuration File Format (`config_*.json`)
   163	
   164	Training configuration files follow the naming pattern `config_*.json`:
   165	
   166	```json
   167	{
   168	  "model_name": "resnet50",
   169	  "dataset": "imagenet-1k",
   170	  "batch_size": 256,
   171	  "learning_rate": 0.1,
   172	  "lr_schedule": "cosine",
   173	  "weight_decay": 0.0001,
   174	  "epochs": 90,
   175	  "optimizer": "sgd",
   176	  "momentum": 0.9,
   177	  "seed": 42
   178	}
   179	```
   180	
   181	These files are used by the anomaly detector to cross-reference declared hyperparameters with observed training behavior.
