docs/formats.md:3:## 1. MLCK Checkpoint Format (`.mlck`)
docs/formats.md:32:| 40 | 8 | int64 | CreationTimestamp | Unix timestamp (seconds) when checkpoint was created |
docs/formats.md:95:| 4 | uint32 | Epoch | Training epoch at checkpoint time |
docs/formats.md:97:| 8 | float64 | LearningRate | Learning rate at checkpoint time |
docs/formats.md:99:| ParentHashLen | bytes | ParentHash | ASCII hex SHA-256 of the parent checkpoint file (for lineage) |
docs/formats.md:150:| `event` | string | Event type: `step`, `epoch_end`, `checkpoint`, `eval` |
docs/analysis_rules.md:27:## 2. Anomaly Detection Rules
docs/analysis_rules.md:49:### 2.3 Learning Rate Anomaly
docs/analysis_rules.md:60:- **Scope**: Between consecutive checkpoints (entries with `event == "checkpoint"` or between .mlck files sorted by epoch/step)
docs/analysis_rules.md:61:- **Trigger**: `acc` drops by more than 0.15 (absolute, not relative) between consecutive checkpoints
docs/analysis_rules.md:63:- **Output fields**: `prev_acc`, `curr_acc`, `drop`, `prev_checkpoint`, `curr_checkpoint`
docs/analysis_rules.md:65:### 2.5 Checkpoint Integrity - Tensor Checksum
docs/analysis_rules.md:72:### 2.6 Checkpoint Integrity - Header Checksum
docs/analysis_rules.md:79:### 2.7 Checkpoint Integrity - Signature
docs/analysis_rules.md:81:- **Method**: For signed checkpoints (Flags bit 0), compute HMAC-SHA256 of bytes [0..SignatureOffset) using SignerId as key, compare with stored signature
docs/analysis_rules.md:88:- **Method**: For each checkpoint with a non-empty `parent_hash`, verify that a checkpoint with that file hash exists in the evidence set
docs/analysis_rules.md:89:- **Trigger**: Parent checkpoint not found
docs/analysis_rules.md:102:- **Method**: Compare `DatasetHash` across all checkpoints in the same lineage chain
docs/analysis_rules.md:157:Each `.mlck` checkpoint file is identified by the SHA-256 hash of its entire file content (hex-encoded).
docs/analysis_rules.md:161:For each checkpoint with a non-empty `ParentHash` in the provenance section:
docs/analysis_rules.md:162:- If a checkpoint with that SHA-256 file hash exists in the evidence set, create a directed edge from parent to child.
docs/analysis_rules.md:163:- If no matching parent is found, the checkpoint is classified as an **orphan**.
