[?2004l[?2004h> new = """### 3.1 Grammar
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ```
[?2004l[?2004h> query      := or_expr
[?2004l[?2004h> or_expr    := and_expr ("OR" and_expr)*
[?2004l[?2004h> and_expr   := not_expr ("AND" not_expr)*
[?2004l[?2004h> not_expr   := "NOT" not_expr | atom
[?2004l[?2004h> atom       := "(" or_expr ")" | condition
[?2004l[?2004h> condition  := field COMP_OP value
[?2004l[?2004h> COMP_OP    := ">" | "<" | ">=" | "<=" | "==" | "!="
[?2004l[?2004h> field      := "step" | "epoch" | "loss" | "lr" | "grad_norm" | "acc" | "event" | "ts"
[?2004l[?2004h> value      := NUMBER | QUOTED_STRING | TIMESTAMP
[?2004l[?2004h> NUMBER     := integer or float literal
[?2004l[?2004h> QUOTED_STRING := '"' ... '"' (double-quoted string)
[?2004l[?2004h> TIMESTAMP  := ISO 8601 format (e.g., 2024-01-15T10:30:00Z)
[?2004l[?2004h> ```
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### 3.2 Operator Precedence
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> - `NOT` is a prefix operator with the highest precedence.
[?2004l[?2004h> - `AND` binds tighter than `OR`.
[?2004l[?2004h> - Parentheses `(` `)` override the default precedence.
[?2004l[?2004h> - Malformed parenthesized queries, such as `(step < 5` or `step < 5)`, are invalid query syntax.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> Examples:
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> - `NOT epoch == 0` parses as `NOT (epoch == 0)`.
[?2004l[?2004h> - `loss > 1.0 OR grad_norm > 5.0 AND epoch == 3` parses as `loss > 1.0 OR (grad_norm > 5.0 AND epoch == 3)`.
[?2004l[?2004h> - `loss > 1.0 OR NOT grad_norm > 5.0 AND epoch == 3` parses as `loss > 1.0 OR ((NOT (grad_norm > 5.0)) AND epoch == 3)`.
