[?2004l[?2004h>       "source": "shard_002.jsonl"
[?2004l[?2004h>     },
[?2004l[?2004h>     {
[?2004l[?2004h>       "id": "ANOM-002",
[?2004l[?2004h>       "type": "tensor_checksum_mismatch",
[?2004l[?2004h>       "severity": "critical",
[?2004l[?2004h>       "details": {
[?2004l[?2004h>         "file": "model_epoch3.mlck",
[?2004l[?2004h>         "tensor_name": "encoder.layer2.weight",
[?2004l[?2004h>         "expected_checksum": "abcd1234...",
[?2004l[?2004h>         "actual_checksum": "efgh5678..."
[?2004l[?2004h>       },
[?2004l[?2004h>       "evidence": {},
[?2004l[?2004h>       "source": "model_epoch3.mlck",
[?2004l[?2004h>       "checkpoint": "model_epoch3.mlck"
[?2004l[?2004h>     }
[?2004l[?2004h>   ],
[?2004l[?2004h>   "summary": {
[?2004l[?2004h>     "total": 5,
[?2004l[?2004h>     "by_severity": {
[?2004l[?2004h>       "critical": 1,
[?2004l[?2004h>       "high": 2,
[?2004l[?2004h>       "medium": 1,
[?2004l[?2004h>       "low": 1
[?2004l[?2004h>     },
[?2004l[?2004h>     "by_type": {
[?2004l[?2004h>       "gradient_spike": 1,
[?2004l[?2004h>       "loss_divergence": 1,
[?2004l[?2004h>       "tensor_checksum_mismatch": 1,
[?2004l[?2004h>       "training_gap": 1,
[?2004l[?2004h>       "lr_anomaly": 1
[?2004l[?2004h>     }
[?2004l[?2004h>   }
[?2004l[?2004h> }
[?2004l[?2004h> ```
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> **Field rules:**
[?2004l[?2004h> - `id`: Sequential ID in format `ANOM-NNN`, assigned in detection order.
[?2004l[?2004h> - `anomalies`: sorted by severity (critical > high > medium > low), then by step/epoch.
[?2004l[?2004h> - `type` values: `gradient_spike`, `loss_divergence`, `lr_anomaly`, `metric_regression`, `tensor_checksum_mismatch`, `header_checksum_mismatch`, `signature_invalid`, `provenance_chain_break`, `training_gap`, `dataset_hash_inconsistency`.
[?2004l[?2004h> - `details`: type-specific fields as defined in `/app/docs/analysis_rules.md`.
[?2004l[?2004h> - `evidence`: sibling of `id`, `type`, `severity`, `details`, and `source`; never nested inside `details`. Timeline-based anomalies include `window_values`, an array of up to 5 preceding metric values at the point of anomaly detection. `gradient_spike` uses preceding `grad_norm` values, `loss_divergence` uses preceding `loss` values, and other timeline-based anomalies may use an empty array when no meaningful preceding window is available. Checkpoint-based anomalies, such as `tensor_checksum_mismatch`, must have an empty evidence object: `{}`.
[?2004l[?2004h> - `source`: the artifact file where the anomaly was detected.
[?2004l[?2004h> - `epoch` and `step`: present only for timeline-based anomalies.
[?2004l[?2004h> - `checkpoint`: present when the anomaly is related to a specific checkpoint file; omitted for timeline-based anomalies that are not checkpoint-specific.
[?2004l[?2004h> - `summary`: reflects the filtered anomaly list when `--filter-severity` is supplied.
[?2004l[?2004h> - If no anomalies are detected, `anomalies` is an empty array.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### Detect CSV Output
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> When `--format csv` is used with `detect`, the command outputs CSV instead of JSON. The CSV header is exactly:
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ```text
[?2004l[?2004h> id,type,severity,epoch,step,source,checkpoint
[?2004l[?2004h> ```
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> One header row is followed by one data row per anomaly. Each data row has 7 comma-separated fields in that order. Leave `epoch`, `step`, or `checkpoint` empty when the anomaly does not have that field. Severity filtering with `--filter-severity LEVEL` applies before CSV output, so the rows reflect only the filtered anomaly list.
[?2004l[?2004h> '''
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> if old not in s:
[?2004l[?2004h>     raise SystemExit('output_schema.md detect section not found')
