    70	- **Trigger**: Mismatch
    71	- **Severity**: `critical`
    72	- **Output fields**: `file`, `tensor_name`, `expected_checksum` (hex), `actual_checksum` (hex)
    73	
    74	### 2.6 Checkpoint Integrity - Header Checksum
    75	
    76	- **Method**: Compute FNV-1a 64-bit of bytes [0..48) and compare with stored value at offset 48
    77	- **Trigger**: Mismatch
    78	- **Severity**: `critical`
    79	- **Output fields**: `file`, `expected_checksum` (hex), `actual_checksum` (hex)
    80	
    81	### 2.7 Checkpoint Integrity - Signature
    82	
    83	- **Method**: For signed checkpoints (Flags bit 0), compute HMAC-SHA256 of bytes [0..SignatureOffset) using SignerId as key, compare with stored signature
    84	- **Trigger**: Mismatch
    85	- **Severity**: `critical`
    86	- **Output fields**: `file`, `signer_id`, `valid` (bool)
    87	
    88	### 2.8 Provenance Chain Break
    89	
    90	- **Method**: For each checkpoint with a non-empty `parent_hash`, verify that a checkpoint with that file hash exists in the evidence set
    91	- **Trigger**: Parent checkpoint not found
    92	- **Severity**: `medium`
    93	- **Output fields**: `file`, `parent_hash`, `found` (bool)
    94	
    95	### 2.9 Training Gap
    96	
    97	- **Method**: Consecutive timeline entries (after merge sort) have timestamps more than 2 hours apart
    98	- **Trigger**: `time_diff > 7200 seconds` between consecutive entries within the same epoch
    99	- **Severity**: `info`
   100	- **Output fields**: `after_step`, `before_step`, `after_ts`, `before_ts`, `gap_seconds`
   101	
   102	### 2.10 Dataset Hash Inconsistency
   103	
   104	- **Method**: Compare `DatasetHash` across all checkpoints in the same lineage chain
   105	- **Trigger**: Different `DatasetHash` values within the same chain
   106	- **Severity**: `high`
   107	- **Output fields**: `files`, `hashes` (list of unique hex hashes)
   108	
   109	---
   110	
