7:## CLI Interface
15:### Commands
27:### Global Flags
31:| `--format` | string | `json` | Output format: `json`, `text`, or `csv` (`csv` is supported only by `detect`) |
34:### Command-Specific Behavior
36:#### `ingest`
43:Output (JSON to stdout): see `/app/docs/output_schema.md` section "Ingest Output".
47:#### `timeline`
56:Output (JSON to stdout): see `/app/docs/output_schema.md` section "Timeline Output".
58:#### `verify`
67:Output (JSON to stdout): see `/app/docs/output_schema.md` section "Verify Output".
69:#### `detect`
79:- `--format csv`: output CSV instead of JSON. The CSV header is exactly `id,type,severity,epoch,step,source,checkpoint`; one data row is emitted per anomaly. Leave `epoch`, `step`, or `checkpoint` empty when the anomaly does not have that field.
80:- `--filter-severity LEVEL`: filter anomalies to show only those at the specified severity level or above. Severity order is `critical > high > medium > low > info`. For example, `--filter-severity high` shows only `critical` and `high` anomalies, while `--filter-severity critical` shows only `critical` anomalies. The returned JSON summary reflects the filtered anomaly list.
82:Output (JSON to stdout): see `/app/docs/output_schema.md` section "Detect Output".
84:#### `lineage`
95:Output (JSON to stdout): see `/app/docs/output_schema.md` section "Lineage Output".
97:#### `query`
105:Output (JSON to stdout): list of matching timeline entries.
107:#### `diff`
113:Compare two checkpoint files inside `<evidence-dir>` tensor by tensor and write JSON to stdout. `file1` and `file2` are checkpoint filenames relative to `<evidence-dir>`.
119:Output (JSON to stdout): see `/app/docs/output_schema.md` section "Diff Output".
121:#### `report`
125:Output (JSON to stdout): see `/app/docs/output_schema.md` section "Report Output".
