docs/spec.md:9:All commands write JSON to stdout unless otherwise specified. Every JSON command output includes a top-level `metadata` object with `tool`, `version`, `command`, `evidence_dir`, and `timestamp` fields. CSV output is not modified and does not include JSON metadata.
docs/spec.md:81:- `--format csv`: output CSV instead of JSON. CSV output remains CSV-only and does not include a JSON `metadata` object. The CSV header is exactly `id,type,severity,epoch,step,source,checkpoint`; one data row is emitted per anomaly. Leave `epoch`, `step`, or `checkpoint` empty when the anomaly does not have that field.
docs/spec.md:125:Generate a comprehensive forensic report by running all analyses (ingest, timeline, verify, detect, lineage) and combining results. The report output includes top-level metadata with `command: "report"`; nested report sections do not include their own metadata objects.
